    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-13352",
      "problem": "What would be a counterexample for the following false statement?\n\n$7n-2$ is even for any $n \\in \\mathbb{Z}$",
      "worked_solution": "Our statement can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14266535/assets/f081609878fffca1966a5a6590a6eb9f5bdc2b458bc14b582bc1b37be8248c9d.svg)\n\nSince this statement is false, its negation is true. \n\nA *counterexample* is a particular case that disproves the statement. Equivalently, it's a case that proves the negation is true. \n\nThe negation of our statement is\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14266535/assets/2b01d5742a9fa72af17e95e4cb9d119f89d8fdfd0030d4613ce99dc5dfd0bf3f.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\nA counterexample for the above statement would be an integer $n$ such that $7n-2$ is odd.",
